{"title":"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621fc87144ca55480bb1ed63f6d000e4e3dea9ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m} - 2^{n} = 1792$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" />. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb40d190ad7572256d2029ed56b046e355ad2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} + n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550751abd3c98c2c27e593dd4a72281cea58e470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> like this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dbcb719864b5b21ad32d4bf1f7193ab8cd6d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n} \\times (\\frac{2^{m}}{2^{n}} - 1) = 1792$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e1029c7746fe689af9b78926f5c0614183e43c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}(2^{m - n} - 1) = 1792$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5800218c4299b9176fbf1a112c0667b61e31a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1792$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c01434bbada4cbaf7837540d9ad0c9240d32828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{8} \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> are both positive integers, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550751abd3c98c2c27e593dd4a72281cea58e470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be even because the base is even, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b758860a3987dc5abce80cf2fdeb96bdd0adc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m - n} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> must be odd. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550751abd3c98c2c27e593dd4a72281cea58e470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be equal to the even part of the prime factorization and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b758860a3987dc5abce80cf2fdeb96bdd0adc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m - n} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> must be equal to the odd part of the prime factorization, like this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bccf60d6a21b35b9ce91747d3199734b7c40a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n} = 2^{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/26858c2becbfe024f2a38f506fce66d56f3e0b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5dba9d61da43f165905af7abde0b5a31bc48675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m - n} - 1 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/26858c2becbfe024f2a38f506fce66d56f3e0b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0140e68ba2f2f53d188eff2a907e0c679786081c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m - 8} - 1 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791ff16796acb98edcffe77d5207801bcfefcb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m - 8} = 7 + 1 = 8 = 2^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c08eb59b552de33d59a1bf519d716f0f2b76c129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - 8 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/73402428783c11196d054b633fa68708c5c1fda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 3 + 8 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e921f405977229521ee7bc3cf5dc0fe3b62cdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/26858c2becbfe024f2a38f506fce66d56f3e0b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb40d190ad7572256d2029ed56b046e355ad2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} + n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16b91756a93fdb89e4655143b4f01c319d575bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11^{2} + 8^{2} = 121 + 64 = \\boxed{185}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"221\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC\">2016 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_5\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 5\">Team Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_7\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 7\">Team Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•